      <img class="text-decoration-right"
        src="/assets/img/Smoky Mountain Acres/text-decoration-half-leaf.webp"
        alt="">
    </div>
    <p>Curious, social, and happiest when they have room to root and explore.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="row gy-4 align-items-center">
      <div class="col-lg-5">
        <img src="/assets/img/9.11.26/pigletsPlaying.webp"
          class="img-fluid"
          alt="Kune Kune pigs eating together at Smoky Mountain Acres">
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-7 content">
        <h3>Kune Kune and Other Pasture Pigs</h3>
        <p>
          Our Kune Kune pigs are friendly, compact, and full of personality. They are well suited to pasture-based living and spend time outdoors rooting, grazing, exploring, and interacting with the herd.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pasture is paired with organic supplemental feed appropriate for growing and adult pigs. We do not make “grass only” claims; responsible pig care means meeting their nutritional needs as pasture and seasons change.
        </p>
        <p>
          Depending on the season and our breeding plans, pigs may be available for pets, homesteads, breeding, or whole-hog meat purchases. Availability, breeds, and pricing change as the farm grows.
        </p>
        <a href="/livestock/" class="offer-link">VIEW LIVESTOCK AVAILABILITY</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="chickens" class="about section paper-texture">
  <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up">
    <div class="row gy-4 align-items-center">
      <div class="col-lg-5 order-lg-2">
        <img src="/assets/img/9.11.26/ChickensInPasture2.webp"
          class="img-fluid"
          alt="Barred Rock chicken at Smoky Mountain Acres">
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-7 order-lg-1 content">
        <h2>CHICKENS</h2>
        <h3>A Pasture-Based Laying Flock</h3>
        <p>
          Our chickens spend their days scratching through grass and leaves, looking for insects, seeds, and plants, and exploring the spaces around their shelters. Their natural foraging is part of farm life, not a substitute for good nutrition.
        </p>
        <p>
          We supplement pasture with organic poultry feed formulated to support the flock's health and egg production. Farm-fresh egg availability depends on daylight, weather, age, molting, season, and what the hens are actually laying.
        </p>
        <p>
          The flock is also a favorite part of a farm visit. Chickens are active, observant, and often quick to investigate visitors who stand still long enough.
        </p>
        <a href="/farm-tours/" class="offer-link">MEET THE FLOCK ON A FARM TOUR</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="sheep" class="featured-services section">
  <div class="container section-title" data-aos="fade-up">
